(i) That he will pay to the Government the rent and the royalties reserved in his licence at the times and in the manner prescribed by this - Act and will work and carry on the operations licensed in a fair, orderly, skillful and workmanlike manner and with as little damage as possible to the surface of the lands over which the licence extends and to the trees, crops, buildings, structures and other property thereon;

